        {
          "id": 435513778,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "Thanks for your comments, @martin.r.mathieson . Do you mean that we should check the key pointers are not NULL before using g_sm_fragment_params_table rather than return 0? We notice that function sm_fragment_hash() from line 376 to line 388 in the same file has similar logic to this function. So I'm wondering if 0 is an appropriate return value in this case?\n\n```\nstatic guint\nsm_fragment_hash(gconstpointer k)\n{\n    const sm_fragment_key* key = (const sm_fragment_key*) k;\n    guint hash_val;\n\n    if (!key || !key->addr_info)\n       return 0;\n\n    hash_val = (wmem_str_hash(key->addr_info) ^ key->id) + key->p2p_dir;\n\n    return hash_val;\n}\n\n```",
          "author": {
            "id": 7465751,
            "username": "XidongWang-coder",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "XidongWang-coder",
            "state": "active",
