    {
      "id": "3941487f24ec34e8f7a0d792b87396d41d0000a3",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 435527728,
          "type": null,
          "body": "I don't see how a NULL key could ever be passed to a call to g_sm_fragment_params_table.  Was there a (fuzzed?) capture file that caused a crash here?",
          "author": {
            "id": 6810036,
            "username": "martin.r.mathieson",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Martin Mathieson",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/030414c33f619ee28811cd9c073802ef2267d160ab2744eb8427bd49af4c7998?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/martin.r.mathieson"
          },
          "created_at": "2020-10-24T17:28:31.147Z",
          "updated_at": "2020-10-24T17:28:31.147Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 75566023,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 704,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "bcf5570d276bec6433ffa818008cbd22766f93a6",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 435542209,
          "type": null,
          "body": "I have to agree that the returning 0 from sm_fragment_hash and the like is the wrong thing to do because 0 is a valid hash value.\n\nThe problem has to be prevented before these functions are called.\n\nHowever, looking at the hash table functions used in epan/reassemble.c I see the following:\n\n```\n                if (fd_head->next != NULL) {\n                        new_key = g_slice_new(reassembled_key);\n                        new_key->frame = pinfo->num;\n                        new_key->id = id;\n                        g_hash_table_insert(table->reassembled_table, new_key, fd_head);\n                }\n```\n\nWhich cannot possibly pass NULL to g_hash_table_insert unless we are out of memory ... maybe there should be an assert there.\n\nThe other place is:\n\n```\n        key = table->persistent_key_func(pinfo, id, data);\n        g_hash_table_insert(table->fragment_table, key, fd_head);\n```\n\nIn this case the only way for a NULL to be passed in would be if your persistent key hash function returns NULL.\n\nSo, the question is: What motivated this new change.\n\nI made the original change based on a change made in another dissector, but I suspect the change was incorrect, now.",
          "author": {
            "id": 903699,
            "username": "realrichardsharpe",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Richard Sharpe",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/2bb6279a40c9fb03ce3532d450742d062039b1ba6fb484775b8c6aadf34e500c?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/realrichardsharpe"
          },
