    {
      "id": "5786244d8d19400547cf8fa9ec4db5e21f124e5c",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 435544006,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "And here is likely the problem. In sm_fragment_temporary_key and sm_fragment_persistent_key we find:\n\n```\n    if (addr == NULL || pinfo->src.data == NULL || pinfo->dst.data == NULL)\n        return NULL;\n```\n\nThis is definitely wrong. If those fields are null, then we must use default values of some sort or cause a malformed packet assert or something like that.",
          "author": {
            "id": 903699,
            "username": "realrichardsharpe",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Richard Sharpe",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/2bb6279a40c9fb03ce3532d450742d062039b1ba6fb484775b8c6aadf34e500c?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/realrichardsharpe"
          },
          "created_at": "2020-10-24T20:07:33.779Z",
          "updated_at": "2020-10-25T01:49:20.603Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 75566023,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 704,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 435570395,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Thanks, this new change is motivated by a static analysis checker reporting potential NULL pointer dereference in sm_fragment_params_hash, which I think is similar to operations in sm_fragment_hash.\n\nSo according to your comment, should we delete the returning 0 operation in sm_fragment_hash() and change the sm_fragment_temporary_key and sm_fragment_persistent_key return value to make sure NULL can't be passed into g_hash_table_insert?",
          "author": {
            "id": 7465751,
            "username": "XidongWang-coder",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "XidongWang-coder",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/3dbd57a944dfa5baa4b77fe291d455e05d5edfec819c21095f92da3894157735?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/XidongWang-coder"
          },
          "created_at": "2020-10-25T01:49:20.547Z",
          "updated_at": "2020-10-25T01:51:27.181Z",
